SplitMind patch 0015 for OpenConnector v1.9.2 (after 0001-0005 and 0009-0014).
Upstream issue: not filed yet.
Email watch: #96 failure loop, #97 quieter run log, #98 gap start, #101 alias reuse, #102 tests and 90-cap log, #119 wider invisible strip.
From cda8ae1948aadcaacc34335410331e92340cfda9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitMind <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:58:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(email-watch): failure loop, gap start, alias reuse,
 quieter run log, invisible strip (#96 #97 #98 #101 #102 #119)

#96: an aborted poll clears catch_up (retried on the normal interval); after 24
hours without a successful read, one pending watch_gap item (rule watch-failing)
per failure streak. #98: the expired-history gap starts at last_success_at.
#101: cursors record an account fingerprint (sha256 of connection id and provider
account id); a different or missing one drops the alias's items and cursor in one
guarded batch, and list/acknowledge hide them (and names with no cursor) until
then. #97: audit "failures" writes no run row for a successful watcher call.
#102: warn with the omitted count past the 90-connection cap; race tests assert
the injection ran. #119: strip every default-ignorable code point, U+2800,
U+20E3 and marks after digits. Migration 0022 adds the cursor columns.
